# rows-page-subject.tflw — CHECK-ONLY FIXTURE (tflw `G10`, `D1384`): a `rows` line asking a finished
# row about a locator — `TF096`. A row is judged after it ends, when its page is closed. The line
# beside it counts the rows' statuses, which a finished row can answer, and checks clean.
#
# Run explicitly (dot-directory — see bad-keyword.tflw's header for why):
#   npx tflw check tests/.checkonly/rows-page-subject.tflw
with each
  | n |
  | 1 |
  | 2 |
test "health {n}"
  api GET /health
  expect status equals 200
rows
  expect every row status equals 200
  expect every row text "Healthy" is visible
